      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary artery dissection occurring after a nonpenetrating chest trauma is extremely rare. We describe herein the case of a 43-year-old man who suffered traumatic myocardial infarction after an intimal tear of the right coronary artery had been inflicted by a horse stepping on his back."},
